I have everything needed. Here's the report.

## 1. `mtgCardShape()` — actually lives in `apps/tabletop/src/server/tableFurniture.ts` (not `shared/tableFurniture.ts` — that path doesn't exist)

`src/server/tableFurniture.ts:106-182`:

```ts
export interface MtgCardShapeArgs {
  id: TLShapeId; pageId: string; x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number;
  index: IndexKey; instanceId: string; scryfallId: string; cardName: string;
  frontImageUrl: string; backImageUrl: string | null;
  face: "front" | "back"; faceDown: boolean; sleeveColor: string | null;
  cardBackImageUrl: string | null; owner: string; isCommander: boolean;
  isLocked?: boolean; opacity?: number;
}

export function mtgCardShape({ id, pageId, x, y, w, h, index, instanceId, scryfallId,
  cardName, frontImageUrl, backImageUrl, face, faceDown, sleeveColor, cardBackImageUrl,
  owner, isCommander, isLocked = false, opacity = 1 }: MtgCardShapeArgs): MtgCardShape {
  return {
    id, typeName: "shape", type: "mtg-card", x, y, rotation: 0, index,
    parentId: pageId as TLPageId, isLocked, opacity,
    props: { w, h, instanceId, scryfallId, cardName, frontImageUrl, backImageUrl,
      face, faceDown, tapped: false, sleeveColor, cardBackImageUrl, owner, isCommander },
    meta: {},
  };
}
```

Note: `gameCardIndex` is NOT a prop of the mint function or `MtgCardShapeProps` (`src/shared/mtgCardShape.ts:5-19`) — it's not persisted on the shape today.

Call sites of `mtgCardShape(`:
- `src/server/cardArrival.ts:129` — `applyCardArrival`, placing a card from `card.played`
- `src/server/seatJoined.ts:158` and `:168` — minting the ghost (locked, opacity 0.3) and real commander card in the command zone

## 2. `apps/tabletop/src/server/server.ts` — routes

- `GET /health` — `server.ts:24`
- `GET /otel-config.json` — `server.ts:28`
- `POST /api/tables/:tableName/events` → `handleSeatJoined` — `server.ts:44`
- `POST /test/tables/:tableName/cards` → `handleTestCardSeed` — `server.ts:49` (only mounted when `ENABLE_TEST_SEED_ROUTE=true`)
- static file serving of `CLIENT_DIR` — `server.ts:52`
- `GET /` → redirect to Shuffler — `server.ts:54`
- `GET /t/:tableSlug` → SPA fallback (`index.html`) — `server.ts:59`
- Plus a raw `ws` upgrade handler at `/connect/:roomSlug` (not an Express route) — `server.ts:79-113`

**How room state is accessed from an Express handler** (`src/server/seatJoined.ts`, the template):

```ts
const entry = getOrCreateRoom(tableName);          // rooms.ts registry lookup
if (!entry.spineSubscription) {
  entry.spineTableId = envelope.tableId;            // spineTableId set here
  entry.spineSubscription = subscribeToSpine(envelope.tableId, ...);
}
...
if (entry.seats.has(seatId)) { ... }                // seats Map keyed by seatId
const playerArea = await ensurePlayerArea(entry, pageId, seatId, playerName, {...});
```

Full `handleSeatJoined` (POST `seat.joined`) as the template, `src/server/seatJoined.ts:36-183`: validates via `validateIncomingEvent`, checks `envelope.tableId` slug matches URL, requires `initiator.seatId`, calls `getOrCreateRoom(tableName)`, dedups on `entry.seenEventIds`/`entry.seats.has(seatId)`, checks `entry.seats.size >= MAX_SEATS`, wraps the mutation in a `tracer.startActiveSpan("add player furniture", ...)`, calls `entry.room.updateStore(store => store.put(...))`, then `entry.seenEventIds.add(envelope.id)` and `res.status(201).json({ ok: true })`.

## 3. `apps/tabletop/src/server/rooms.ts` — registry shape

`RoomEntry` (`rooms.ts:45-68`):
```ts
export interface RoomEntry {
  tableName: string;
  room: TLSocketRoom<TLRecord>;
  seenEventIds: Set<string>;
  seats: Map<string, PlayerArea>;   // seatId -> PlayerArea
  createdAt: Date;
  hasInstance(instanceId: string): boolean;
  spineTableId?: string;
  spineSubscription?: SpineSubscription;
}
```
`PlayerArea` (`rooms.ts:24-42`) holds `seatIndex`, `playerName`, `playmatImageUrl?`, `cardBackImageUrl?`, `sleeveColor?`, `primaryColor?`, `secondaryColor?`, `graveyardCount`, `stackCount`, `commanderNames`, `damageCounterCount`.

Access pattern: `getOrCreateRoom(tableName: string): RoomEntry` (`rooms.ts:79-105`) is the sole entry point — keyed by the opaque table slug in module-level `const registry = new Map<string, RoomEntry>()` (`rooms.ts:77`). From a handler: `entry.spineTableId` directly; a seat's `playerName` via `entry.seats.get(seatId)?.playerName` (or `entry.seats.get(seatId).playerName` after a `.has()` guard, as `handleSeatJoined` does).

## 4. `apps/tabletop/src/client/TablePage.tsx`

`TLComponents` object (`TablePage.tsx:114-117`):
```ts
const components: TLComponents = {
  Toolbar: ToolbarWithCounter,
  ContextMenu: TableContextMenu,
};
```

**Client-side fetch pattern for calling the Tabletop's own server routes**: there is currently **no production client-side fetch call** to `/api/tables/:tableName/events` (seat.joined) — that POST is made by the *Shuffler*, not by Tabletop client code. Grepping `src/client` for `fetch(` only turns up `src/client/observability/index.ts` (OTel exporters). The only place inside `apps/tabletop` that POSTs `seat.joined`/card events over HTTP against the Tabletop server is **test code**: Playwright helpers in `test/verification/helpers.ts` use `page.request.post(`${baseURL}/api/tables/${tableSlug}/events`, { data: seatJoined(...) })` and `page.request.post(`${baseURL}/test/tables/${tableSlug}/cards`, { data: event })`. Server-to-Spine (not Tabletop-server) calls use a bare `fetch` — see `sendCardReturnedToSpineBestEffort` in item 6 below — which is server-side (`src/server/sendCardReturned.ts`), not client-side, despite being triggered by a client drag gesture; nothing on this ship yet shows a client → own-server fetch helper to copy.

## 5. `cardArrival.ts` and `gameCardIndex` availability

There is no `apps/tabletop/src/client/shapes/cardArrival.ts`; the arrival logic is server-side: `apps/tabletop/src/server/cardArrival.ts`.

`CardPlayedPayload` (`cardArrival.ts:14-24`) declares `gameCardIndex?: number` on the wire payload, but the destructure that pulls fields out of `envelope.payload` (`cardArrival.ts:52`) omits it:
```ts
const { card, face, zoneHint, frontImageUrl, backImageUrl, cardName, owner, isCommander } = envelope.payload;
```
So `gameCardIndex` **is present on the incoming `card.played` envelope** (`envelope.payload.gameCardIndex`) at the point `applyCardArrival` runs, but it is currently dropped — never read, never passed into `mtgCardShape(...)` (`cardArrival.ts:129-142`), and not a field of `MtgCardShapeProps`/`MtgCardShapeArgs` at all. It would need to be added to the destructure, to `MtgCardShapeArgs`/`mtgCardShape`, and to `MtgCardShapeProps` (`src/shared/mtgCardShape.ts`) to persist on the shape. Compare `sendCardReturned.ts`'s `CardReturnedParams.gameCardIndex: number` (required, not optional) — that's the existing consumer of a card's `gameCardIndex`, currently threaded in by the caller rather than read off the shape (since the shape doesn't carry it).

## 6. Test files

- `zoneHitTest.ts` (`src/client/shapes/zoneHitTest.ts`) and `cardZoneEntry.ts` (`src/client/shapes/cardZoneEntry.ts`) — **no dedicated unit test files exist**. Grepping `test/` and `src/` for `zoneHitTest|cardZoneEntry` only turns up their own imports (`MtgZoneShapeUtil.tsx`, `MtgCardShapeUtil.tsx`, and each other). Zone-entry/drag behavior is covered only at the Playwright level: `test/verification/verify-zone-entry.spec.ts`.
- `sendCardReturned.ts` → `test/sendCardReturned.test.ts` (vitest, unit-style, no fake editor needed since this module is a pure server-side HTTP sender). Style: spins up a real `http.createServer` fake Spine (`createFakeSpineServer()`, listens on port 0, records requests, can be told to fail with a status), then asserts the POSTed envelope against the real JSON Schemas in `../../contracts` via `ajv` (`Ajv2020` + `ajv-formats`), and separately asserts it never throws when the Spine is unreachable or rejects (best-effort). No MSW; hand-rolled `http` server instead.
- Playwright dir: `apps/tabletop/test/verification/` (config likely points `baseURL` there; run via `./verify.sh` per `CLAUDE.md`). Shared helpers: `test/verification/helpers.ts` — `openTable`, `zoomToFit`, `joinSeat`, `placeCard` (seeds a card via the test-only `POST /test/tables/:tableSlug/cards` route, after calling `joinSeat`), `center`, `dragPointTo`, `dragCenterTo`, `dragCardTo(page, card, targetSelector)` (`helpers.ts:127-130`, drags a card Locator onto a target selector's center) — directly reusable as a template for "drag a card onto a zone."
- **Best existing template for "drag a card onto a zone"**: `test/verification/verify-zone-entry.spec.ts` — uses `placeCard` to seed a card, locates zone shapes by `[data-shape-id="shape:region-graveyard-${tableSlug}-e2e-seat"]` / `...-exile-...`, calls `dragCardTo(page, card, graveyard)`, then asserts the card's shape element is centered inside the zone's bounding box via a custom `isCenteredIn` helper polled with `expect(...).toPass({ timeout: 5000 })`.
- The removed prototype spec (`git show origin/prototype/portal-gesture-ticket-04:apps/tabletop/test/verification/verify-portal-prototype.spec.ts`) still exists on that branch. It builds its own local `cardPlayed(overrides)` envelope (not using the shared helper — this predates `test/verification/helpers.ts`'s `cardPlayed`), POSTs to (an older) `POST /api/tables/:tableSlug/cards` test-seed route, then does raw `page.mouse.move/down/move/up` drag sequences over a `library` zone locator (`[data-shape-id="shape:library-${tableSlug}-e2e-seat"]`) asserting `page.getByTestId("portal-arming")` attaches/detaches and the card locator detaches (`not.toBeAttached`) once "swallowed." It also covers a multi-select group-drag variant, dragging via rubber-band-select (not click, since `mtg-card` treats a click as tap-to-rotate) then a single mouse drag from one selected card's position onto the zone. Useful as an example of asserting arming/drop state via `data-testid`, and of multi-select drag mechanics, even though its route and helper style are now superseded by `test/verification/helpers.ts`.
